From: Alex Henrie <alexhenrie24@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Fix length computation in RtlUpcaseUnicodeStringToOemString.

Backported from WineHQ commit 6987ca475f (wine-11.18) without code
changes.

The two lengths differ when the ANSI and OEM code pages encode the string to
a different number of bytes.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/rtlstr.c b/dlls/ntdll/rtlstr.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/rtlstr.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/rtlstr.c
@@ -823,7 +823,7 @@
                                                    BOOLEAN doalloc )
 {
     NTSTATUS ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
-    DWORD len = RtlUnicodeStringToAnsiSize( uni );
+    DWORD len = RtlUnicodeStringToOemSize( uni );
 
     oem->Length = len - 1;
     if (doalloc)
